          "code": "CSR_SURVEY_SENTIMENT_ANALYSIS",
          "id": "1766146185869",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766146185872_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Context\nA survey can be created and sent out to people within the organization. After the survey is completed, sentiment analysis shall be performed on the survey responses with results as positive, neutral, or negative. The sentiment analysis will identify the potential topics from the survey question/responses and then conduct sentiment analysis for those topics.\n\n### Instruction\nGiven the input data {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.surveydata}} in JSON format as follows:\n{\n    \"survey_question\": \"<survey question text>\",\n    \"survey_responses\": [\n        {\n            \"responder_id\": \"<id of the responder>\",\n            \"survey_response\": \"<survey response text>\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\nThe sentiment analysis will identify the potential topics from the survey question/responses and then conduct sentiment analysis for those topics. A topic should be a noun or noun phrase.\n\nWhen extracting topics, select the most relevant noun or noun phrase that directly corresponds to the subject of the survey question. Do not use general terms or synonyms if a more specific noun phrase is present. Only extract topics that are clearly discussed in either the survey question or response.\n\n**You must NEVER use “work”, “colleagues”, “talented”, or any similar general, generic, or abstract words as topics, even if they appear in the survey question or response. Only select topics that refer to a specific process, policy, object, or initiative. If “work”, “colleagues”, “talented,\" or any similar term appears in your list of topics, discard them before producing the final output—even if no other topic remains.**\n\nDo not include more than 3 topics per response.\n\nAssign sentiment strictly based on the respondent’s actual opinion, and use ‘neutral’ if the sentiment is not clearly positive or negative.\n\n### Input Format\nInput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format.\n{\n    \"survey_question\": \"<survey question text>\",\n    \"survey_responses\": [\n        {\n            \"responder_id\": \"<id of the responder>\",\n            \"survey_response\": \"<survey response text>\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\nThe survey question is the attribute \"survey_question\".  \nThe survey responses are an array in the attribute \"survey_responses\".  \nEach object in \"survey_responses\" has an attribute \"responder_id\" and an attribute \"survey_response\" which is the survey response text.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\nFirst, identify the potential topics from the survey question or response, then provide the sentiment for each identified topic.  \nTopic should be a noun or noun phrase like \"presentation\", \"java skills\", \"leadership\", \"trust\", etc.  \n**Do not use topics like \"talented\", \"colleagues\", \"work\", or similarly generic words. Discard these topics before producing your output, and do not return them even if nothing else remains.**    \nDo not include more than 3 topics.\n\nExamples for topic extraction—specificity required:\n\n\"company policies\" (correct) vs. \"policies\" (incorrect)\n\"team meetings\" (correct) vs. \"meetings\" (incorrect)\n\"workspace lighting\" (correct) vs. \"lighting\" (incorrect)\n\"office snacks\" (correct) vs. \"snacks\" (incorrect)\n\"website usability\" (correct) vs. \"usability\" (incorrect)\nDo not give any explanation, only respond with the valid JSON object. Make sure the JSON is valid without any extra words, commas, emojis, or backticks like ```json.\n\n### Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format under a results key:\n    {\n        \"results\": [\n            {\n                \"topic\": \"<insert the topic name>\",\n                \"responder_id\": \"<insert the responder id>\",\n                \"sentiment\": \"<insert the sentiment, which shall be positive, negative or neutral>\"\n            }\n        ]\n    }"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
